error[L0414]: `1` cannot have type `a`
 --> check/generic_literal_errors.rslisp:3:16
  |
3 | (defn pick (x) 1)
  |                ^ this literal has type `a`
  |
  = note: `a` has no trait, so it can be any type, including `string`
  = help: give `a` a numeric trait in the signature

error[L0441]: `300` does not fit every type `n` can be
 --> check/generic_literal_errors.rslisp:8:21
  |
8 | (defn bump (x) (+ x 300))
  |                     ^^^ `n` can be `i8`, which cannot hold this value
  |
  = note: `n` can be any of: i8, i16, i32, i64, i128, isize, u8, u16, u32, u64, u128, usize, f32, f64
  = help: narrow `n` with a trait whose types all hold this value

